[sm5y+@andrew.cmu.edu (Samuel Antonio Minter) writes:]
[] What exactly is wizard mode??  I gather it is diferent from discovery mode.

normal mode: very challenging game with scores posted.
discover mode: challenging game but you can confirm/deny your death, no
    scores are posted and you get a wand of wishing to start.
wizard mode: also known as debug mode: you get special commands to map
    floors, create monsters, teleport, etc. all in the name of finding
    bugs. to this end you also get unlimited intrinsic wishing. the games
    maintainer uses this mode to trouble-shoot the game. it is never
    intended to be used by the public, however circumstances may favor
    certain instances of the game beign released with the wizard known.

[] So how do you get to wizard mode on the PC version (from linc)?

dunno, however don't feel that you need to know the wizard's name in order
to get to the special commands so that you can make some sense of the game.
you don't need wizard mode in order to be able play successfully. discover
mode is fine and intelligent play is requisite!

it's upto the compiler/distributor to provide or not provide the wizard
name. so stay tuned since i believe they're listening ...

